# Word → site copy

Yes — the user may supply project (or insight) copy as a **Word `.docx`**. Read the file and map meaning into content. Do **not** paste Word casing blindly onto the site.

## Expected Word layout (per project)

1. **Project name** → `title`
2. **Description** → tagline / summary
3. **Project type** → involvement id (`end-to-end` / `contribution` / `specialized`)

项目详情 body always: Background → Challenge → What I did → Outcome (English when both languages are present).

## Display casing (mandatory — use judgment)

Word may be all-lowercase for speed. **On the site, polish:**

- **Titles:** Title Case — capitalize each major word (e.g. `Mass Effect Tali Companion Bundle`). Do **not** leave all-lowercase; do **not** force CSS `text-transform: uppercase` on project titles unless the design system already requires it for a specific label style.
- **Taglines / short descriptions:** Sentence case (e.g. `Found your home with Tali?`).
- **Involvement / article type chips:** CSS `text-transform: uppercase` — small labels are all caps (FK Grotesk Mono).
- Brand / character names keep correct proper nouns (Mass Effect, Tali, etc.).

## Known bug — fixed

Insight **Related** cards need visible type chips on the dark detail page — use `.insight-detail .insight-chip` light-on-dark styles (same idea as `.insights-page .insight-chip`). Do not leave default light-theme chip colors on `#000`.
